1. Aim
To write a Python program to demonstrate the use of the re (Regular Expression) module for pattern matching and searching operations in Python.

2. Algorithm
Start the program.

Import the re module.

Declare a string containing some text.

Use re.search() to search for a specific pattern.

Use re.findall() to find all occurrences of a pattern.

Use re.sub() to replace a matching pattern.

Use re.match() to check whether a pattern occurs at the beginning of the string.

Display the results.

Stop the program.
